  "findings": [
    "Six role/state material inputs resolve to the same neutral grey V2 texture, eliminating the authored rail > armor > channel hierarchy.",
    "The V2 channel texture is around twice the installed channel value. The native central recess changes from17.23 to36.09 while the rail remains near70, reducing relief.",
    "The native full wall top becomes slightly brighter, not darker, while its value standard deviation falls. Dark interior structural mass also brightens substantially.",
    "The same V2 paint has weaker spatial value variation and loses the original subtle blue-grey palette. Resampling reduces texture standard deviation slightly but is not the principal cause.",
    "Sand becomes lighter and grass darker in the paired dome views. Their separate palette changes affect scene brightness perception.",
    "Do not raise global lighting to compensate; restore material role values first."
  ],
  "recommendedTargetsFinalRgb": {
    "armor": [
      48,
      52,
      56
    ],
    "rail": [
